id: pm-gh1759
title: "GH-1759: strict health accepts a merge fence from an enclosing repository for a separate linked worktree"
description: "Reported in GH-1759 against 2026.11.19. auditMergeAttributeFence (src/sdk/merge/install.ts) looks for the managed .gitattributes block by walking filesystem parents of the tracker root up to eight levels, and it does not stop at the active Git worktree root. When a linked worktree of one repository is checked out inside a different repository that has a stale matching fence, the walk finds the outer file. Git never reads attributes above its own top level, so git check-attr reports merge unspecified, yet pm health --strict-exit reports ok with no warnings and exits 0. pm validate and the workspace position read use the same audit. The fix bounds the walk at the active Git worktree root, keeping support for several trackers inside one repository (pm-kynkl8) and the per-worktree driver isolation of GH-1306 (pm-c1dwbt)."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[6]: "area:merge",false-success,"gh:1759",health,merge-fence,worktree
created_at: "2026-11-20T04:44:11.213Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-20T06:35:54.361Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-20T05:12:56.767Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-20T05:12:56.767Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: "A matching managed fence in a .gitattributes above the active Git worktree root never counts: strict health reports merge_fence_missing and exits 1 for a linked worktree with no own fence; An installed fence at the linked worktree root still passes strict health, and a fence inside the same repository between the root and the tracker still counts; pm validate and the workspace position read use the same bounded audit; a tracker outside any Git repository keeps today's bounded walk; A real-Git regression test reproduces the GH-1759 layout and checks both git check-attr and strict health"
parent: pm-o2kc
risk: low
confidence: high
severity: high
resolution: "auditMergeAttributeFence takes an optional gitWorkspaceRoot (resolved from the tracker root when omitted, null keeps the old walk) and stops its .gitattributes walk at that top level, comparing each walked directory by real path so a symlinked tracker path keeps its patterns. pm health, pm validate and the workspace position read pass the root they already resolve. MERGE_SAFETY.md documents the bound; the SDK surface snapshot acknowledges the new parameter."
expected_result: "A linked worktree without its own fence fails strict health with merge_fence_missing even when an enclosing, different repository carries a matching fence; an inner fence and an in-repository nested fence still pass."
actual_result: "The GH-1759 reproduction against this branch's dist exits 1 with failed_because merge_fence_missing:1 while git check-attr reports merge unspecified; restoring the inner fence gives exit 0, ok true, 0 warnings. The real-Git spec passes and fails without the boundary (negative control); the full suite passes (13447 tests)."
component: merge
