comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-20T04:46:55.032Z","harness:claude-code","Investigation note: auditMergeAttributeFence walks up to eight filesystem parents of the tracker root and accepts the first .gitattributes holding a managed block, with no Git-root bound. All three callers share it: health (resolveMergeFenceHealthEvidence), validate (validate_merge_fence_drift) and the workspace position read. Plan: an optional gitWorkspaceRoot bound, compared by realpath per level so a symlinked logical path keeps its tracker-relative patterns; directories outside the bound are never read. Callers pass the git root they already resolve; a tracker outside Git keeps the bounded walk."
  "2026-11-20T04:50:13.037Z","harness:claude-code","Evidence: the GH-1759 shell reproduction against this branch's dist now reports git check-attr merge unspecified, strict health exit 1 with failed_because merge_fence_missing:1; restoring the inner fence gives exit 0, ok true, 0 warnings. The new real-Git spec covers that layout, a fence in an in-repository directory between the root and the tracker (still counted), a symlinked logical tracker path (same fence, same patterns), a boundary that does not hold the tracker, and an unresolvable tracker directory. Negative control: with the boundary check disabled both tests fail at the not_installed expectation (the outer fence is accepted as ok)."
  "2026-11-20T05:34:32.129Z","harness:claude-code","Codex review (gpt-6.2-sol, xhigh) of the first head raised five fence findings, all reproduced and fixed. (1) The logical walk could climb a symlink inside the worktree that points back at its root into the link's own parents (repo/sub/loop -> repo), where a stale sub/.gitattributes matched; the walk now follows the tracker's canonical path to the worktree's canonical top level, and patterns are computed from that ancestry. (2) Git stopped following in-tree .gitattributes symlinks in 2.32; the audit now reads only regular files there (lstat) and continues past a symlinked one. (3) A caller-supplied gitWorkspaceRoot is canonicalized, so a symlinked or 8.3-spelled root no longer yields a false not_installed. (4) findGitWorkspaceRoot stripped trailing spaces from Git's output with trim(); a worktree named with a trailing space then resolved to null and the default audit fell back to the unbounded walk; only the line terminator is stripped now. (5) Containment is judged by native path components rather than the backslash-normalizing isPathOutsideRoot. Inside Git the eight-level cap no longer applies (the walk ends at the top level), so a tracker nine levels down finds the root fence; outside Git the cap stays. Each case has a spec in fence-worktree-boundary.spec.ts."
  "2026-11-20T05:51:56.256Z","harness:claude-code","Codex review round 2 (gpt-6.2-sol, xhigh): three more findings fixed. (1) pm merge install followed a symlinked .gitattributes and reported unchanged when its target already held the block, while the audit (correctly) reports not_installed there, so the prescribed repair could not repair; reconcileGitattributesBlock now treats a symlinked file as changed, and the atomic rename replaces the link with a regular file holding the target's lines, leaving the target untouched (dry run reports changed). (2)+(3) Git path output is now parsed by one helper, stripGitPathTerminator, which removes exactly one LF (CRLF on Windows, where a name cannot hold a CR) for the show-toplevel, absolute-git-dir and driver-scope queries; resolveMergeDriverConfigScope asks for --git-dir and --git-common-dir in separate queries, so a clone whose name ends in a line break stays an ordinary clone with --local drivers instead of being misread as a linked worktree. Specs cover each; with the old combined parsing the line-break clone gains extensions.worktreeConfig (negative control)."
  "2026-11-20T06:02:37.383Z","harness:claude-code","Codex review round 3 found no new defect in the fixes; one scope note recorded as a decision, not changed. Git's check-in attribute lookup falls back to the index when the working-tree .gitattributes is absent or (since 2.32) a symlink it refuses to open, so with a committed regular fence replaced by an unstaged symlink, git check-attr still reports pm-item-toon while the filesystem-only audit reports merge_fence_missing. That outcome is fail-closed, pm merge install resolves it by writing a regular file, and the audit never modelled the index fallback (a deleted but still indexed .gitattributes behaves the same way, before and after this change). The GH-1759 defect was a false success; modelling the index would add Git object reads to every health and validate run for a transient unstaged state."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-20T06:35:54.361Z","harness:claude-code","Shipped in PR #1760, merged to main as 4ff1d83a7 on 2026-11-20 after 32/32 hosted checks passed, CodeRabbit full review (no actionable comments), Greptile 5/5 and three Codex gpt-6.2-sol xhigh rounds; the GitHub issue closed on merge and its blocker_retry run skipped (one release per day held). Reaches users in the next daily release after 2026.11.20."
